# Benchmark Results
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
results/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json

# NuGet lock files are a RECORD, not a pin. Versions float on purpose (the policy lives in
# Directory.Packages.props), so packages.lock.json holds "which exact version did this
# restore resolve" -- useful locally, wrong as a source of truth. It is a local artifact and
# is never tracked: `dotnet publish` writes RID-specific entries (Microsoft.DotNet.ILCompiler)
# into it, so a committed lock dirtied the tree on every release. RestorePackagesWithLockFile
# stays true (restore still writes the record, at every level); .github/workflows/ci.yml
# uploads those files as the `resolved-versions` artifact, so "which versions did that build
# use" is answerable without a file in git.
packages.lock.json
**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
**/[Pp]ackages/*
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
*.nuget.props
*.nuget.targets

